#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135171 :tutorial/content "A **rational expression** is, roughly speaking, an algebraic expression that's in the form of a fraction, or contains fractions.\n\nTo evaluate a rational expression like\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 6 x\n$$\n\nfor $x=2$, all we need to do is replace $x$ with $2$ in the above expression and simplify as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{x} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "12656f01-d648-56e1-9a11-2f5bb03056ec" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8008 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
